WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.932
Hello, I’m Robert Schaub.

2
00:00:02.072 --> 00:00:07.208
I spent 38 years in software engineering and project leadership—30 years at Phonak/Sonova.

3
00:00:07.348 --> 00:00:10.348
I founded FactHarbor Verein, a Swiss non-profit,

4
00:00:10.488 --> 00:00:12.421
and built two foundations:

5
00:00:12.561 --> 00:00:15.561
FactHarbor’s evidence-based fact-checking application, now in Alpha,

6
00:00:15.701 --> 00:00:19.769
and Our AI Charter Runtime’s runnable decision-gateway proof of concept.

7
00:00:19.909 --> 00:00:23.977
My motivation is societal: facts are a foundation of democracy.

8
00:00:24.117 --> 00:00:28.185
I want AI to strengthen, not weaken, responsibility for decisions.

9
00:00:28.325 --> 00:00:32.749
Evidence is essential, but a consequential answer also needs valid authority,

10
00:00:32.889 --> 00:00:38.025
a decision before effect, and a record affected people can inspect and challenge.

11
00:00:38.165 --> 00:00:42.233
FactHarbor’s Alpha assesses public claims against supporting and opposing evidence.

12
00:00:42.373 --> 00:00:46.441
Here is one report already produced by the public Alpha.

13
00:00:46.581 --> 00:00:50.649
It examines a blanket heat-pump recommendation for a Winterthur home

14
00:00:50.789 --> 00:00:55.924
and records evidence for and against, sources, limitations, uncertainty and the resulting verdict.

15
00:00:56.064 --> 00:01:00.132
For the prototype, selected claims will be analysed in advance

16
00:01:00.272 --> 00:01:03.629
and their reports stored for the decision gateway.

17
00:01:03.769 --> 00:01:06.769
Evidence-Gated Agents will test the next step.

18
00:01:06.909 --> 00:01:11.333
An AI may draft an exact answer from those stored reports,

19
00:01:11.473 --> 00:01:17.676
but a gateway outside the model decides whether current authority and declared evidence support its release.

20
00:01:17.816 --> 00:01:20.817
If the gateway blocks a proposed answer,

21
00:01:20.957 --> 00:01:26.804
the request may be narrowed and a new answer prepared from current authority and evidence.

22
00:01:26.944 --> 00:01:31.012
The new proposal must pass every check again before release.

23
00:01:31.152 --> 00:01:34.508
If released, the recipient receives an inspectable receipt

24
00:01:34.648 --> 00:01:38.004
linking the answer, authority, evidence, decision and outcome.

25
00:01:38.144 --> 00:01:42.924
Beyond the prototype, I want to develop evidence-gated decision-making applications and services

26
00:01:43.064 --> 00:01:46.421
for companies, public bodies, newsrooms and civil society.

27
00:01:46.561 --> 00:01:52.052
With permission, they could weigh an organisation’s policies, contracts and records alongside public evidence.

28
00:01:52.192 --> 00:01:57.328
People affected by an answer should be able to understand it, challenge it,

29
00:01:57.468 --> 00:02:00.112
and seek correction or independent review.

30
00:02:00.252 --> 00:02:03.964
I built both foundations and can integrate them directly.

31
00:02:04.104 --> 00:02:09.596
The Prototype Fund’s coaches and cohort can challenge my assumptions, improve the recipient experience,

32
00:02:09.736 --> 00:02:14.872
and help me reach practitioners who can test whether the receipt is understandable

33
00:02:15.012 --> 00:02:18.724
and where AI adds justified value over simpler methods.

34
00:02:18.864 --> 00:02:24.000
My vision is a free and fair society in which technology strengthens democracy

35
00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:28.208
because consequential decisions remain authorised, evidence-grounded and open to challenge.
